      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep, that looks to match what I had in mind.\n\nI don\u0027t think we have to move away from correlation by name for `Pinout` entries, but an option I\u0027d like to keep open is the `Contacts` property, e.g:\n\n```\n{\n   \"Name\": \"J12\",\n   \"Type\": \"Port\",\n   \"PortType\": \"connecting\",\n   \"FormFactor\": \"Ext Port\",\n   \"Pinout\": [\n       {\n           \"Type\": \"Bus\",\n           \"Name\": \"I2C\",\n           \"Protocol\": \"I2C\",\n           \"Contacts\": {\n               \"SCL\": 5,\n               \"SDA\": 6,\n           },\n           \"Segment\": \"I2C12.1\"\n       },\n       { ... }\n   ]\n}```\n\nWhere the contact value is a specific pin index.\n\nBut I don\u0027t think it\u0027s necessary that we do that yet, just that we don\u0027t preclude ourselves from doing it later (as an escape hatch).",
